# 29. Important Data Science Concept — Data Leakage 🚨

This is one of the most important things we'll begin learning early.

Suppose you're predicting:

> Whether a customer will default on a loan.

You accidentally include:

```text
loan_recovery_status
```

which is only known **after** the loan default occurs.

Your model may perform amazingly during testing.

But in production:

```text
Prediction time
       ↓
recovery_status doesn't exist yet
```

Therefore the model cannot actually use it.

This is **data leakage**.

### Core principle

> **A feature must be legitimately available at prediction time.**

We'll revisit this repeatedly throughout your ML training.

---

# 30. Train/Test Leakage

Another important issue.

Suppose you calculate preprocessing statistics using the entire dataset before splitting:

```text
Train + Test
     ↓
Calculate mean
     ↓
Transform everything
     ↓
Split
```

The test set has influenced the preprocessing.

Better:

```text
Dataset
  ↓
Split
 ┌────────┐
Train    Test
 ↓
Fit preprocessing
 ↓
Transform Train
 ↓
Transform Test using
Train-fitted parameters
```

This becomes extremely important when we study:

**Scikit-learn Pipelines.**

